WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.320
Right, let's go to Russia.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.440
Let's go to Russia!

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.870
Russia.

00:00:07.939 --> 00:00:11.190
If you're a British tourist, Russia isn't
easy to get into.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.400
You have to book your travel,

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.509
then request a formal invitation from the
hotel you're staying at,

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:18.520
and then apply for a visa weeks or months
in advance.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.720
You can't just arrive on a plane and ask them
to let you in.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:27.430
And you certainly can't ever, ever just drive
across the border.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.689
That pole is where they're spying from.

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:34.270
Oh, you're right! They must-- yes!

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.360
'Cos that is lumpy at the top.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.270
Cell towers normally go right at the top...

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:39.640
There is going to be someone who job is

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:45.120
counting the cars in and counting the cars
out.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:45.220
And if they see anyone walking towards here...

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.690
Yeah, of course. That's where the cameras
are. Good spot.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.470
I'd get my zoom lens out, but I'm not doing
that on a Russian border.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:53.780
The area behind me is the Saatse Boot,

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.420
and it's about one square kilometre of Russia
that juts out into Estonia.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.730
When Estonia was part of the Soviet Union,
that wasn't a problem:

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.360
but when the country became independent in
1991,

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.330
a couple of villages on this side of the Boot,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.280
including Saatse here, were cut off. Until
recently,

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.080
the road over there was the only way to reach
them:

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.260
there is another way round now,

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.080
but that's still the quickest route by far.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.400
So, for convenience, Russia allows people
to use that road...

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.920
as long as they don't stop.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:22.710
That's the no stopping sign.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.430
Yeah. No stopping for... 1km?

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.390
Right, you see that post, the red and green
post?

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.790
-- I do. -- That's it. That's Russia.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.570
If you're on foot, you're entering Russia,
and you can be arrested.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:34.700
If you're in a car, you've got to keep moving:

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.720
if you stop or if you break down,

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.350
you're entering Russia, and you can be arrested.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.430
Estonia... Estonia...

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.310
-- Russia! -- We're in Russia.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.939
And I know, immediately, people are going
to ask, how far can you push this?

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:50.630
What happens if you're on a bicycle?

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:54.640
What if you drive 1mph but don't technically
stop?

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.170
What happens if you stand half in and half
out,

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:01.049
or stop just on the Estonian side of the border
and take loads of photos?

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:05.250
What happens if you break the law on promoting
homosexuality in Russia

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:10.579
by playing the Village People out of your
car's speakers at full blast?

00:02:10.579 --> 00:02:14.069
The answer to all of those is: I don't know.

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:17.639
It depends on if any border guards see it,
and how they feel that day.

00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:20.489
They might just escort you back to Estonia...

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:23.319
they might arrest you and lock you up for
the night.

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:25.529
Either way, we are not bloody finding out,

00:02:25.529 --> 00:02:29.319
because it is a really, really bad idea to
mess with Russia at all,

00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:32.010
let alone on their territory, while you're
filming it.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.879
Now, at some point, like many of the complicated
borders in the world,

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:36.319
the Boot is going to be fixed.

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:38.579
Officially, it was fixed and handed over to
Estonia

00:02:38.579 --> 00:02:44.090
in a treaty back in 2005, and then again by
another treaty in 2014.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.279
Russia agreed to give up that bit of land

00:02:46.279 --> 00:02:49.849
in exchange for getting a couple of bits of
Estonia somewhere else.

00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:52.060
And... Estonia!

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.370
-- That's it! -- Yeah!

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:59.669
But diplomacy is slow, and so is government
bureaucracy, and right now,

00:02:59.669 --> 00:03:04.870
it is still possible to drive through a little
bit of Russia without a visa.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.059
Just very very carefully.

00:03:07.059 --> 00:03:10.079
We just drove through Russia without a visa!

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:11.619
Wow.

00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:14.949
It's actually a bit of an anticlimax.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.440
Hello! Tourist. Tourist. Yes.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.060
